Subject: [PATCH] Fix the backported openat2 declaration for tar's older gnulib

Ubuntu's CVE-2025-45582 backport copies a four-argument _GL_FUNCDECL_SYS
call into tar 1.35, whose macro takes three arguments. Join the attributes
to the parameter list, as the existing declarations in that gnulib do.
Keep the nonnull attributes and all the upstream path-security code.

--- a/gnu/fcntl.in.h
+++ b/gnu/fcntl.in.h
@@ -273,4 +273,4 @@
 _GL_FUNCDECL_SYS (openat2, int,
                   (int fd, char const *file, struct open_how const *how,
-                   size_t size),
+                   size_t size)
                   _GL_ARG_NONNULL ((2, 3)));
